.TH UBXCTL 1 "November 2026" "ubxctl 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
ubxctl \- terminal tool for configuring UBX GNSS receivers (unofficial)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ubxctl
.RB [ \-p
.IR port ]
.RB [ \-b
.IR baud ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B ubxctl
is a terminal user interface for configuring u\-blox generation 9 and later GNSS
receivers over a serial or USB port.
It is an independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed by u\-blox AG.
.PP
The tabs show the fix, satellites and RF status, every configuration key in the RAM,
BBR, Flash and default layers, message output rates, a raw message console, and tools
to save, clear, export and import configuration and to restart the receiver.
Status is read by polling once a second, so viewing it doesn't change the receiver's
configuration.
Edits go to the RAM layer unless BBR or Flash is chosen.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-p " port\fR, " \-\-port " port"
Serial port.
Without it, ubxctl uses the first u\-blox USB device, else the first FTDI, CP210x,
CH340 or PL2303 USB serial adapter.
.TP
.BI \-b " baud\fR, " \-\-baud " baud"
Baud rate.
Without it, ubxctl tries the common rates and keeps the first one the receiver answers on.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short usage message.
.SH KEYS
.TP
.B 1 \fR...\fP 6
Switch to the Status, Satellites, Configuration, Messages, Console or Tools tab.
.TP
.B r
Reload the configuration from the receiver.
.TP
.B p
Pause or resume status polling.
.TP
.B o
Reset the trip distance.
.TP
.B q
Quit.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I /usr/share/ubxctl/ubxctl/presets/
Presets offered by Tools \(-> Import, in the same
.RI \(lq CFG\-NAME " value" \(rq
format as Tools \(-> Export.
.SH NOTES
On Linux, if
.BR gpsd (8)
is using the port, ubxctl stops it before opening the port.
A systemd gpsd is stopped with
.B sudo systemctl
and started again when ubxctl exits; a gpsd started by hand is sent SIGTERM and not
restarted.
Any other program holding the port stops ubxctl from starting.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR gpsd (8)
.PP
https://github.com/shawcx/ubxctl
